From: BC-250 SteamOS Real Toolkit
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: force a link re-detect after a long display blank (amdgpu.cs_relink_*)

Ported from MastaG/linux-cachyos-bc250 patches/linux-cachyos/0011-cs-relink-after-long-blank.patch
to Valve's SteamOS kernel 7.2 tree. Applied by build.sh inside the --dsc
block (PCON/HDMI 2.1 feature group).

The CH7218-class DP->HDMI 2.1 converter drops its HDMI side when the stream
has been off longer than a few seconds (KDE <-> gamescope handover). DC then
brings the stream back from cached caps, every step reports success, and the
sink stays dark until a hotplug. This patch records when the stream goes
down and, if it comes back after longer than cs_relink_ms (default 3000),
runs the trigger_hotplug sequence shortly after the commit completes.

Runtime tunables (module params):
  amdgpu.cs_relink_ms=3000            blank length that triggers a re-detect, 0 = off
  amdgpu.cs_relink_delay_ms=250       how long after the commit to run it
  amdgpu.cs_relink_cooldown_ms=10000  minimum spacing between re-detects
  amdgpu.cs_relink_at_boot=0          also re-detect once on the first bring-up
  amdgpu.cs_relink_debug=1            log arm / run / skip

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm.c
@@ -97,6 +97,402 @@
 #include <drm/drm_audio_component.h>
 #include <drm/drm_colorop.h>
 #include <drm/drm_gem_atomic_helper.h>
+#include <drm/drm_probe_helper.h>
+
+/*
+ * BC-250: force a link re-detect after a long display blank.
+ *
+ * The board drives HDMI through a DP->HDMI 2.1 converter (Chrontel CH7218).
+ * When the display stream has been off for more than a few seconds -- a slow
+ * compositor handover, e.g. switching between a desktop session and gamescope
+ * -- the converter drops its HDMI side. DC then brings the stream back from
+ * *cached* link caps and converter info: it never calls link_detect, so the DP
+ * side trains, DSC is enabled, the mode is committed, every step reports
+ * success, and the sink stays dark. Only a hotplug recovers it.
+ *
+ * So: remember when the stream went down, and if it comes back after longer
+ * than cs_relink_ms, run the same re-detect the trigger_hotplug debugfs file
+ * does, shortly after the commit completes.
+ *
+ * It cannot be done inline. The recovery needs drm_modeset_lock_all(), which
+ * the atomic commit path already holds -- hence the delayed work.
+ *
+ * Deliberately NOT driven off the converter's DPCD readiness bits
+ * (DP_PCON_HDMI_TX_LINK_STATUS 0x303b, DP_PCON_HDMI_POST_FRL_STATUS 0x3036):
+ * this adapter reads 0x00 in both even on a healthy link with a picture, so
+ * anything gated on them fires unconditionally. An earlier attempt built on
+ * them looped every ~4.4 s and visibly flickered the TV. Elapsed time is the
+ * only trigger shown to discriminate, and cs_relink_cooldown_ms is a hard loop
+ * breaker on top of it.
+ */
+/*
+ * Blank length that triggers a re-detect.
+ *
+ * 3000 rather than something tighter because a re-detect is not free: it
+ * releases and recreates the sink, so it costs a real modeset. Measured on
+ * this hardware, every blank that recovered on its own was <= 3.32 s and every
+ * blank that went dark was >= 4.44 s, so 3000 sits below every observed
+ * failure while leaving the ordinary 0.1-2.1 s handovers alone. An earlier
+ * default of 1000 fired on 1.8 s and 2.1 s session switches that were
+ * perfectly healthy, which was worse than doing nothing.
+ */
+static uint cs_relink_ms = 3000;
+module_param(cs_relink_ms, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(cs_relink_ms,
+		 "BC-250: re-detect the link when a display stream has been off longer than this many ms (0 = disabled)");
+
+static uint cs_relink_delay_ms = 250;
+module_param(cs_relink_delay_ms, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(cs_relink_delay_ms,
+		 "BC-250: how long after a commit to run the forced link re-detect, in ms");
+
+static uint cs_relink_cooldown_ms = 10000;
+module_param(cs_relink_cooldown_ms, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(cs_relink_cooldown_ms,
+		 "BC-250: minimum time between two forced link re-detects, in ms");
+
+static bool cs_relink_debug = true;
+module_param(cs_relink_debug, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(cs_relink_debug,
+		 "BC-250: log when a forced link re-detect is armed, run or skipped");
+
+/*
+ * Also re-detect once on the first bring-up of a boot.
+ *
+ * The rest of this mechanism only ever sees blanks that happen while the
+ * driver is running: cs_relink_off_at is set when a stream goes down, so the
+ * very first bring-up of a boot has nothing to measure and would otherwise be
+ * skipped. A machine that boots with the converter already in the dropped
+ * state therefore gets no help at all -- reported from the field, surviving
+ * several reboots before clearing on its own.
+ *
+ * Whether a second detect actually clears that state is genuinely unknown. DC
+ * already runs a full link_detect during startup, roughly three seconds before
+ * the first mode is committed, so this may well just repeat it to no effect;
+ * and nothing here can tell a dropped converter from a healthy one, because
+ * this adapter's DPCD readiness bits read 0x00 in both cases.
+ *
+ * OFF by default, because it is not free. dc_link_detect() releases and
+ * recreates link->local_sink, so amdgpu_dm_update_connector_after_detect()
+ * sees a new sink and drives a real modeset plus a hotplug uevent -- not a
+ * passive probe. Doing that 250 ms into every boot, for an unproven benefit,
+ * is not a trade worth making for everyone.
+ *
+ * Enable it only to investigate a machine that boots black. Look for the
+ * "first bring-up" line in dmesg to see what it decided.
+ */
+static bool cs_relink_at_boot;
+module_param(cs_relink_at_boot, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(cs_relink_at_boot,
+		 "BC-250: also force one link re-detect on the first bring-up after boot (0 = disabled (default), 1 = enabled)");
+
+/*
+ * How long after boot a bring-up still counts as "the first one".
+ *
+ * Without a bound the one shot is spent whenever a stream first appears on the
+ * converter, which on a board powered up before its TV can be hours later --
+ * forcing a redundant modeset just as the user's picture arrives. It also
+ * retires the shot if the parameters are toggled at runtime long after boot.
+ */
+#define CS_RELINK_BOOT_WINDOW_MS 60000U
+
+static void cs_relink_work_fn(struct work_struct *work);
+static DECLARE_DELAYED_WORK(cs_relink_work, cs_relink_work_fn);
+
+/*
+ * Written from the atomic commit path, read by cs_relink_work_fn. The commit
+ * path is serialised against itself and the work only ever runs one at a time,
+ * so no extra locking is needed here.
+ */
+static struct drm_connector *cs_relink_connector;
+static unsigned long cs_relink_off_at;		/* jiffies; 0 = nothing pending */
+static bool cs_relink_boot_pending = true;	/* first bring-up not seen yet */
+static bool cs_relink_is_boot_run;		/* the run in flight is the boot shot */
+static unsigned long cs_relink_last_run;	/* jiffies; 0 = never run */
+static bool cs_relink_armed;
+static bool cs_relink_running;			/* recovery in flight */
+
+/*
+ * Is this stream going out through a DP->HDMI converter?
+ *
+ * On the BC-250 this is answered by dpcd_caps.dongle_type, which reads
+ * DISPLAY_DONGLE_DP_HDMI_CONVERTER -- confirmed on hardware, not assumed. A DP
+ * port carrying an HDMI signal is also accepted, as belt and braces for a
+ * converter that does not report a dongle type; on this board that arm never
+ * fires, because DC labels the stream SIGNAL_TYPE_DISPLAY_PORT and treats the
+ * converter as transparent.
+ */
+static bool cs_relink_stream_is_pcon(const struct dc_stream_state *stream)
+{
+	const struct dc_link *link;
+
+	if (!stream)
+		return false;
+
+	link = stream->link;
+	if (!link)
+		return false;
+
+	if (link->connector_signal == SIGNAL_TYPE_DISPLAY_PORT &&
+	    dc_is_hdmi_signal(stream->signal))
+		return true;
+
+	return link->dpcd_caps.dongle_type == DISPLAY_DONGLE_DP_HDMI_CONVERTER ||
+	       link->dpcd_caps.dongle_type == DISPLAY_DONGLE_DP_HDMI_DONGLE;
+}
+
+/*
+ * Called just before the old stream is released, i.e. as the display goes down.
+ *
+ * The timestamp is recorded unconditionally rather than only for a converter
+ * link: whether the recovery is wanted is decided when the display comes back,
+ * where the incoming stream is in hand. Gating here as well only adds a way for
+ * the mechanism to be silently inert.
+ */
+static void cs_relink_note_stream_off(const struct dc_stream_state *stream)
+{
+	if (!cs_relink_ms || cs_relink_running)
+		return;
+
+	/* 0 means "nothing pending", so never store it. */
+	cs_relink_off_at = jiffies ? jiffies : 1;
+
+	/* A measured blank exists from here on, so the boot case is over. */
+	cs_relink_boot_pending = false;
+
+	if (cs_relink_debug && stream && stream->link)
+		pr_info("bc250 relink: stream down (signal=%d connector_signal=%d dongle_type=%d pcon=%d)\n",
+			stream->signal, stream->link->connector_signal,
+			stream->link->dpcd_caps.dongle_type,
+			cs_relink_stream_is_pcon(stream));
+}
+
+/* Called just before the new streams are committed, i.e. as the display returns. */
+static void cs_relink_arm_if_needed(struct drm_device *dev,
+				    const struct dc_commit_streams_params *params)
+{
+	struct drm_connector_list_iter iter;
+	struct drm_connector *connector;
+	struct dc_link *link = NULL;
+	bool first_bringup;
+	unsigned int off_ms;
+	int i;
+
+	if (!cs_relink_ms || cs_relink_running)
+		return;
+
+	/*
+	 * No measured blank means this is the first bring-up of the boot. There
+	 * is nothing to time, so it only qualifies when explicitly opted into,
+	 * and then only once, and only while it still plausibly is the boot.
+	 */
+	first_bringup = !cs_relink_off_at;
+	if (first_bringup && cs_relink_boot_pending &&
+	    time_after(jiffies, (unsigned long)INITIAL_JIFFIES +
+			        msecs_to_jiffies(CS_RELINK_BOOT_WINDOW_MS))) {
+		cs_relink_boot_pending = false;
+		if (cs_relink_debug)
+			pr_info("bc250 relink: first stream on the converter came %u ms after boot, outside the %u ms boot window - not re-detecting\n",
+				jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - (unsigned long)INITIAL_JIFFIES),
+				CS_RELINK_BOOT_WINDOW_MS);
+	}
+	if (first_bringup) {
+		if (!cs_relink_boot_pending)
+			return;			/* already spent or retired */
+
+		if (!cs_relink_at_boot) {
+			/* Decline once and stay quiet for the rest of the boot.
+			 * This also means enabling the parameter at runtime
+			 * cannot arm a re-detect out of nowhere.
+			 */
+			cs_relink_boot_pending = false;
+			if (cs_relink_debug)
+				pr_info("bc250 relink: first bring-up of this boot at %u ms; cs_relink_at_boot=0, leaving the link alone\n",
+					jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - (unsigned long)INITIAL_JIFFIES));
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * Only a commit that actually brings a stream up on the converter
+	 * consumes the timestamp. A commit that merely tears the display down
+	 * must leave it alone -- it is the one that just set it, and the blank
+	 * being measured runs from that commit to a later one. Clearing it
+	 * unconditionally here made every multi-commit blank measure ~0 ms
+	 * against itself, which is the whole case this patch exists for.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < params->stream_count; i++) {
+		if (cs_relink_stream_is_pcon(params->streams[i])) {
+			link = params->streams[i]->link;
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+
+	if (!link) {
+		if (cs_relink_debug)
+			pr_info("bc250 relink: commit with %d stream(s), none on a converter - nothing consumed\n",
+				params->stream_count);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	if (first_bringup) {
+		/* One shot, whether or not it ends up arming below. */
+		cs_relink_boot_pending = false;
+		cs_relink_is_boot_run = true;
+		off_ms = cs_relink_ms;
+		if (cs_relink_debug)
+			pr_info("bc250 relink: first bring-up of this boot at %u ms, forcing a re-detect (cs_relink_at_boot=1)\n",
+				jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - (unsigned long)INITIAL_JIFFIES));
+	} else {
+		cs_relink_is_boot_run = false;
+		off_ms = jiffies_to_msecs(jiffies - cs_relink_off_at);
+		cs_relink_off_at = 0;
+
+		if (off_ms < cs_relink_ms) {
+			if (cs_relink_debug)
+				pr_info("bc250 relink: blank was %u ms, under the %u ms threshold\n",
+					off_ms, cs_relink_ms);
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+
+	if (cs_relink_last_run &&
+	    time_before(jiffies,
+			cs_relink_last_run + msecs_to_jiffies(cs_relink_cooldown_ms))) {
+		if (cs_relink_debug)
+			pr_info("bc250 relink: blank was %u ms but a re-detect ran less than %u ms ago, not re-arming\n",
+				off_ms, cs_relink_cooldown_ms);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	drm_connector_list_iter_begin(dev, &iter);
+	drm_for_each_connector_iter(connector, &iter) {
+		struct amdgpu_dm_connector *aconnector;
+
+		if (connector->connector_type == DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_WRITEBACK)
+			continue;
+
+		aconnector = to_amdgpu_dm_connector(connector);
+		if (aconnector->dc_link != link || aconnector->mst_root)
+			continue;
+
+		cs_relink_connector = connector;
+		cs_relink_armed = true;
+		break;
+	}
+	drm_connector_list_iter_end(&iter);
+
+	if (cs_relink_debug)
+		pr_info("bc250 relink: blank was %u ms (>= %u ms) - %s\n",
+			off_ms, cs_relink_ms,
+			cs_relink_armed ? "arming a forced re-detect"
+					: "no connector matched the link, nothing to do");
+}
+
+static void cs_relink_schedule_if_armed(void)
+{
+	if (!cs_relink_armed)
+		return;
+
+	cs_relink_armed = false;
+	cs_relink_running = true;
+
+	if (cs_relink_debug)
+		pr_info("bc250 relink: running the %s re-detect in %u ms\n",
+			cs_relink_is_boot_run ? "boot" : "blank", cs_relink_delay_ms);
+
+	schedule_delayed_work(&cs_relink_work,
+			      msecs_to_jiffies(cs_relink_delay_ms));
+}
+
+/*
+ * The recovery itself: the trigger_hotplug debugfs sequence, which is the only
+ * thing measured to bring the picture back once the converter has dropped its
+ * HDMI side. It runs from a workqueue precisely so drm_modeset_lock_all() below
+ * is not taken underneath the atomic commit that armed it.
+ */
+static void cs_relink_work_fn(struct work_struct *work)
+{
+	struct drm_connector *connector = cs_relink_connector;
+	enum dc_connection_type new_connection_type = dc_connection_none;
+	struct amdgpu_dm_connector *aconnector;
+	struct amdgpu_device *adev;
+	struct drm_device *dev;
+	const char *outcome;
+	bool detected;
+
+	if (!connector) {
+		outcome = "no connector";
+		goto done;
+	}
+
+	aconnector = to_amdgpu_dm_connector(connector);
+	if (!aconnector->dc_link || aconnector->mst_root) {
+		outcome = "connector went away";
+		goto done;
+	}
+
+	dev = connector->dev;
+	adev = drm_to_adev(dev);
+
+	if (amdgpu_in_reset(adev)) {
+		outcome = "GPU in reset";
+		goto done;
+	}
+
+	mutex_lock(&aconnector->hpd_lock);
+
+	if (!dc_link_detect_connection_type(aconnector->dc_link, &new_connection_type) ||
+	    new_connection_type == dc_connection_none) {
+		mutex_unlock(&aconnector->hpd_lock);
+		outcome = "connection type probe failed";
+		goto done;
+	}
+
+	mutex_lock(&adev->dm.dc_lock);
+	detected = dc_link_detect(aconnector->dc_link, DETECT_REASON_HPD);
+	mutex_unlock(&adev->dm.dc_lock);
+
+	if (!detected) {
+		mutex_unlock(&aconnector->hpd_lock);
+		outcome = "dc_link_detect failed";
+		goto done;
+	}
+
+	amdgpu_dm_update_connector_after_detect(aconnector);
+
+	drm_modeset_lock_all(dev);
+	dm_restore_drm_connector_state(dev, connector);
+	drm_modeset_unlock_all(dev);
+
+	drm_kms_helper_connector_hotplug_event(connector);
+
+	mutex_unlock(&aconnector->hpd_lock);
+
+	outcome = "done";
+
+done:
+	/*
+	 * Stamp the cooldown even on the failure paths: a re-detect that cannot
+	 * complete will not complete any better if it is retried immediately,
+	 * and this is the only thing standing between a bad probe and a loop.
+	 *
+	 * Except for the boot shot. That one is speculative and already
+	 * one-shot by construction, so letting it start the clock would refuse
+	 * the first genuine long blank of the boot -- which is the case this
+	 * mechanism actually exists for, and which lands well inside the
+	 * cooldown on a normal startup.
+	 */
+	if (!cs_relink_is_boot_run)
+		cs_relink_last_run = jiffies ? jiffies : 1;
+	cs_relink_connector = NULL;
+	cs_relink_off_at = 0;
+	cs_relink_running = false;
+
+	if (cs_relink_debug)
+		pr_info("bc250 relink: %s re-detect: %s\n",
+			cs_relink_is_boot_run ? "boot" : "blank", outcome);
+}
 
 #include <media/cec-notifier.h>
 #include <acpi/video.h>
@@ -2430,6 +2826,11 @@
 {
 	int i;
 
+	/* BC-250: the relink work holds a bare connector pointer. */
+	cancel_delayed_work_sync(&cs_relink_work);
+	cs_relink_connector = NULL;
+	cs_relink_running = false;
+
 	if (adev->dm.vblank_control_workqueue) {
 		destroy_workqueue(adev->dm.vblank_control_workqueue);
 		adev->dm.vblank_control_workqueue = NULL;
@@ -11177,6 +11578,8 @@
 		    (!new_crtc_state->active ||
 		     drm_atomic_crtc_needs_modeset(new_crtc_state))) {
 			manage_dm_interrupts(adev, acrtc, NULL);
+			/* BC-250: note it before the release may free the stream. */
+			cs_relink_note_stream_off(dm_old_crtc_state->stream);
 			dc_stream_release(dm_old_crtc_state->stream);
 		}
 	}
@@ -11277,6 +11680,11 @@
 			flush_workqueue(dm->vblank_control_workqueue);
 	}
 
+	/* BC-250: decide whether this bring-up follows a blank long enough to
+	 * have lost the converter's HDMI side.
+	 */
+	cs_relink_arm_if_needed(dev, &params);
+
 	dm_enable_per_frame_crtc_master_sync(dc_state);
 	mutex_lock(&dm->dc_lock);
 	dc_exit_ips_for_hw_access(dm->dc);
@@ -11870,6 +12278,9 @@
 	/* Signal HW programming completion */
 	drm_atomic_helper_commit_hw_done(state);
 
+	/* BC-250: run the forced re-detect once the modeset locks are gone. */
+	cs_relink_schedule_if_armed();
+
 	if (wait_for_vblank)
 		drm_atomic_helper_wait_for_flip_done(dev, state);
 
